  "evidence_quotes": [
    "The Bible is not a book contain info about a world but is a world - in fact the only true actual world - + this real world shows up here in this maya world as a book",
    "This ur-realization on your part; it was not accidental. It was in fact his plan. yet nonetheless it depended on a choice you made of your own free will",
    "the meta-abstraction is, basically, a realization that what was taken to be two things is in fact one thing seen twice, at two times + places; but is not this perception of what I call 'common essence' even beyond Plato's Forms",
    "the total unified reality field (which is our universe experienced as an integrated oneness a unity) is not in itself ultimate reality, but, when perceived (correctly) in this unified way, leads to an inferrential awareness of something further",
    "the universe - reality field - is its body, we see only the body, + yet paradoxically, that body is only seeming, so what we experience is only seeming, but what we know inferentially by its perturbation of that body is real"
  ],
